					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-05-11 | Friday</font></strong><br><br><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">Today has arrived. Most give thanks only when a journey is over. I&#39;ll do it before this new one begins. Thanks do <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">DJ daps1</span> for grinding out some video work for the album release (and who will also be spinning tonight). Thanks to <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Zia</span> for the shotgun filming and editing sessions through out the marathon. Thanks for all the video drops, Seattle. Thanks to the organizers and working class champions who balance patience and necessity in a cold world. Thanks to family - the first collective.</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; min-height: 14px; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; min-height: 14px; margin: 0px"><span class="Apple-style-span">Damn. It&#39;s an honor to share the stage with <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Black Anger</span> tonight. That Dude <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Larry Mizell</span> pretty much <a href="http://www.thestranger.com/seattle/Content?oid=219280">summed up my sentiments in his column in The Stranger this week.</a></span></p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; min-height: 14px; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">Big up to the local media folkers for the airtime: <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">KEXP</span>, B-Mello and Taybot at Street Sounds, J Moore and DJ Hyphen at Sunday Night Soundsessions (<span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">KUBE</span>), <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">KJR-950</span>&#39;s Mike Gastineau (aka The Gasman) and the good folks at 104.5, <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">KBCS</span> 91.3 and <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">KUOW</span> 91.1. Lastly, Saba and I will be hitting up <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">KNDD</span> 107.7 at around 1pm for a last push to promote tonight and tomorrow&#39;s shows and the upcoming album. </p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; min-height: 14px; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">Peace to the courageous Iraqi people resisting foreign domination. Peace to the good and young of our country who are being led to the sandtrap. No peace to the puppetmasters who still win, even when both sides lose. </p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; min-height: 14px; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">Isulong! to the <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">KABATAAN Partylist</span> representing the progressive voice of the youth and students in the Philippines - elections May 14!  </p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; min-height: 14px; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">206, 360, 425, 253 and the greater Northwest, let&#39;s show &#39;em what we got. </p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-05-10 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br><object width="425" height="350" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" data="http://www.vimeo.com/moogaloop.swf?clip_id=187219"><br /><param name="movie" value="http://www.vimeo.com/moogaloop.swf?clip_id=187219"></param><br /><param name="wmode" value="transparent"></param><br /></object>thaswassup.<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-05-09 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/217/491914207_8802fa978d.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="432" height="288" /><br /><br />^^^Blue Scholars are just as excited as you are to see Black Anger perform live at this weekend&#39;s &quot;Bayani&quot; release party.<br /><br />Seattle weather has been unusually filthy for the past few days. Just in time for rising gas prices. Speaking of gas, advance shout-outs to the showbox hotdog vendors, or as George Lopez calls them...&quot;wieners&quot;. Speaking of vendors, make sure to cop 3 Bayani albums when it comes out. Speaking of cops, the NAACP is investigating the OPAs findings concerning the SPDs still crooked ways. Speaking of acronyms, Text BACK (Brigade Against Cheating and Killings) is a worldwide campaign for Filipinos to text a message to friends/relatives back home and encourage them to vote for progressive partylists in the upcoming elections. Represent your right to text back, text back, text back, <a href="http://blog.myspace.com/index.cfm?fuseaction=blog.view&amp;friendID=129352359&amp;blogID=262660681&amp;MyToken=28fcfda4-a245-4b64-b6be-bf096213a2e7">text back</a>.<br /><br />BAYANI,<br />daps1<br /><br /><em>*photo by daps1</em><br /><br /><br /> <p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-05-07 | Monday</font></strong><br><br>(her little brother&#39;s twin, Marrakech, Morrocco)<br /><br />shouts to MassLine representative <strong>Nissana</strong> for snapping flicks of young folks reppin <strong>Blue Scholars</strong> across the world. <br /><br />made us think. hm. anybody and everybody who has MassLine relevant pictures should email them to me at (sabzi at bluescholars dot com) and we&#39;ll get them featured somehow on the site.<br /><br />thaswassup!<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-05-05 | Saturday</font></strong><br><br>salutations, comrades.&nbsp; i&#39;m very honored to announce the long-awaited arrival of my goddaughter, nina (9lbs. 4oz. -- 21in.).&nbsp;&nbsp; isn&#39;t she lovely?&nbsp;&nbsp; isn&#39;t she special?&nbsp;&nbsp; perfect in every way, my dude.&nbsp;&nbsp; congratulations to the homie deuce and his wife aimee on the new addition (no NE heartbreak).&nbsp;&nbsp; i got status, y&#39;all -- now bow and kiss the ring.<br /><br />for me, nina&#39;s birth is&nbsp;especially poignant, bringing with it some solace&nbsp;when considering just how many lives are lost on the daily, whether in baghdad, kabul,&nbsp;darfur or detroit.&nbsp; i&nbsp;continue to re-emphasize the point because i see tremendous value in the internalization:&nbsp; life is precious; our time here with one another is short; show respect and be of service to your peoples.<br /><br />speaking of respect, much is due to the ASB at redmond high school for putting together an impressive showcase of organizational skill at last night&#39;s &quot;redmond live!&quot;&nbsp;&nbsp; big up&#39;s to the homie jared and his support staff for makin&#39; it happen.&nbsp;&nbsp; keep your search engines running for some truly amazing footage of your massliners in action -- not only hard at work, but hard at play, too (sabzi&#39;s got sprints, cousin!).<br /><br />one more congratulatory shout out to matt and jackie, who&#39;ll be attending the prom together next month.&nbsp;&nbsp; oh, what a night...<br /><br />in love and service,<br /><br />RA<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> [35] <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive